    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (the only runnable test class is `AcceptanceTest`; the other two files are a base class and a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner whose lower-cased email duplicates any existing owner's, responding with **409 Conflict**, following the existing `isTelephoneInUse` pattern:\n\n1. **`ClinicService`** (interface) \u2014 added `boolean isEmailInUse(String email)` with Javadoc mirroring the sibling uniqueness checks.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 implemented `isEmailInUse`: returns `false` for a null email, otherwise lower-cases the candidate and every stored owner's email (via a private `normalizeEmail` helper using `Locale.ROOT`) and checks for a match. Annotated `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` like the others.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added the conflict check right after the telephone check, returning `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` when the email is already in use. The owner's email is already lower-cased at this point by `OwnerMapper.toOwner`, and the service normalizes both sides again for safety.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes, and the full build is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
