    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing idioms:\n\n- `isEmailInUse` is placed right beside its sibling `isTelephoneInUse` and copies its exact shape (guard on null-normalized input, then `findAll().stream().map(normalize).anyMatch`). A maintainer would find this immediately familiar.\n- The new `normalizeEmail` private static helper mirrors the existing `normalizeTelephone`/`normalizeHousehold*` helpers, keeping normalization logic in one small, well-named unit rather than inlined.\n- The interface Javadoc matches the house style of the neighboring method docs (explaining the normalization/collision semantics).\n- The controller guard is dropped into the existing sequence of `isXInUse` \u2192 `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` checks in `addOwner`, consistent with the telephone/household guards right above it.\n\nNothing is duplicated beyond the deliberate parallelism that already characterizes these sibling checks, and no class or method is turned into a catch-all. Logic sits at the right layer (service enforces the invariant, controller maps to 409).",
